<Layout title="Profile — Salim Youssef Najim" description="Meet Salim Youssef Najim, an Aerospace Engineering student at Khalifa University building across engineering, entrepreneurship and creative ideas.">
  <section class="page-hero split-hero section-pad"><div><p class="eyebrow section-index">Profile / Salim Youssef Najim</p><h1>Curiosity,<br/><span>put to work.</span></h1><p class="lead">I study Aerospace Engineering at Khalifa University, build engineering projects and approach ideas with a business mindset.</p></div><figure class="portrait-frame"><img src="/images/salim.webp" alt="Portrait of Salim Youssef Najim" width="826" height="826" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption class="eyebrow">The person behind the work</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section class="chapter-section section-pad"><p class="eyebrow section-index">An evolving perspective</p><div class="chapters"><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">01</span><div><h2>An engineering foundation.</h2><p>Aerospace is my academic path. It brings together the subjects that draw me in: flight, physics and the way complex systems work.</p><a class="text-link" href="/aerospace/">Explore aerospace <Arrow/></a></div></article><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">02</span><div><h2>Learning through building.</h2><p>For LUMOS, I led a team developing a decentralized urban lighting concept around sustainable energy. The project explored wind generation, storage, a wireless energy transfer demonstration and light sensing.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/lumos/">Explore LUMOS <Arrow/></a></div></article><article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><div><h2>A business perspective.</h2><p>I’m interested in what happens beyond an idea: who it serves, how it works and what it takes to build it. Engineering and entrepreneurship give me different ways to ask those questions.</p><a class="text-link" href="/ventures/">The venture perspective <Arrow/></a></div></article></div></section><ContactCta/>
</Layout>
